A||N||7||kornholio||adding fog lights on SE or GT||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||11-02-1999||08:51 PM||||Has anyone added fog lights to their SE's or GT's?  Is the mounting hard to do?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||11-02-1999||10:18 PM||||I have lights on my 86SE there isn't much frame or metal on tht fascias to mount them out far enough but custom made brackets made long enough from the frame will work this is the way I did mine. where do you want to mount them?||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||11-02-1999||10:33 PM||||I mounted some on my 86SE behind the front fascia. They were mounted on a steel plate that hangs down and they were poining between the bumper and the lower ground effects. I made brackets to hold them in the proper position. Looked almost factory.||||reg||3
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||11-03-1999||12:25 AM||||NO SCCA, That's how I mounted mine. Don't be tell'n people about my car. <P>I guess you said it better than I did.||||reg||10
Z||000004||kornholio||11-03-1999||05:19 AM||||DXR_DAD,<BR>I want to mount eliptical (I think that's how you spell it) style lights between the bumper and the ground effect.  The area SE's and GT's only have on the front fascia.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bill Osmer||11-03-1999||10:33 AM||||Can you guys get pictures of your installations? Those of us that are thinking of similar installations may want to copy (you know imitation is the most sincerest form of praise)or gnerate our modifications.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||11-03-1999||10:33 AM||||Buddies in my Club...Fiero's West...mounted the slim rectangular foglights in the opening of the turn signals of the bumper... They eliminate the turn signals and substitute it with a pair of motorcycle tail signals mounted behind the mouth opening of the bumper...looks great..almost looks like factory...there is an aftermarket chin spoiler for the GT bumper that has a foglight mounting...it's only available for the round type foglights...||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||11-03-1999||09:54 PM||||If you reach in were the license plate is mounted about 8" you will feel a metal frame ta the top. There was two even bolt holes one on each side of the plate that I used. The brackets need to stick out as far as you want the lights to be.||||reg||4
